# Files that ship as they are stored, byte for byte, whatever the system they are checked out on:
# the licence texts the packages carry beside the binary, the presets, and the translation tables,
# several of which are the original FxSound's own files, CRLF and all. `-text` keeps git from
# converting their line ends on checkout and on commit whatever core.autocrlf says, so that a
# Windows checkout (Git for Windows' default is core.autocrlf=true, and GitHub's Windows images
# keep it) packs what the Linux packages pack; packaging/windows/build-windows.ps1 checks the files
# it packs against the commit. Nothing else changes: this is no renormalisation, and every file
# keeps the line ends it is stored with.
/LICENSE -text
/crates/fxsound-rnnoise/COPYING -text
/assets/fonts/OFL*.txt -text
/assets/presets/** -text
/assets/translations/** -text
